    "title": "Kennesaw State is dancing again. Here is who they will play in NCAA Tournament",
    "text": "The Owls will look to pull off a major upset as a No. 14 seed. KENNESAW, Ga. — As the brackets were revealed on Selection Sunday, Kennesaw State found out their seeding and who they will play in the first round of the NCAA Tournament. The Owls were penciled in as a No. 14 seed in the West Region of the bracket and will take on No. 3 seed Gonzaga on Thursday in Portland, Oregon. The Cinderella-hopeful Owls will look to accomplish a feat that's been done 23 times in tournament history before -- knock off a No. 3 seed and advance to the weekend. They awaited their fate inside the VyStar Arena with fans piling in to wait for the announcement. They erupted with excitement when their seeding and opponent was announced. The most recent win by a 14 seed came in 2024, Oakland knocked off Kentucky. Georgia State even produced some of their own magic as a No. 14 seed when they upset the Baylor Bears under head coach Ron Hunter. The Mercer Bears were another team out of the state of Georgia to beat a No. 3 seed -- they did so in 2014 with a massive upset over blueblood Duke and Coach K. The Georgia Bulldogs were upset as a 3 seed by UT Chattanooga in 1997. The lowest seed to ever win an NCAA Tournament was No. 8 Villanova in 1985.",
